<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>New project — OVHcloud Reports</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/app.css">
</head>
<body>
<%- include('_nav', { userName, active: '' }) %>
<div class="app-body">
  <div class="page-header">
    <div>
      <a href="/" class="back-link">← Projects</a>
      <h1 class="page-title">New project</h1>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="form-card">
    <% if (error) { %><div class="auth-error"><%= error %></div><% } %>
    <form method="POST" action="/projects">
      <div class="field-group">
        <label class="field-step" for="name"><span class="step-num">1.</span> Give your project a name <span class="optional">(you'll be able to rename it later on)</span></label>
        <input class="field-input" type="text" id="name" name="name" placeholder="Private boot M1" required autofocus>
      </div>
      <div class="field-group">
        <label class="field-step" for="jira_root_epic"><span class="step-num">2.</span> Fill in the master epic (LVL2) <span class="optional">(also editable later)</span></label>
        <input class="field-input" type="text" id="jira_root_epic" name="jira_root_epic" placeholder="LVL2-9365" required>
        <p class="field-hint">This is the top-level epic your project rolls up to in Jira. Its "End date" field is read automatically to set the Target ETA — you don't fill that in yourself.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="field-group">
        <label class="field-step" for="confluence_url"><span class="step-num">3.</span> Paste the URL of your project's Confluence page</label>
        <div class="format-callout">
          ⚠ This only works if your page follows a specific structure — it is <strong>not</strong> free-form.
          <a href="https://confluence.ovhcloud.tools/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=994384126" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Start from the template page →</a>
        </div>
        <input class="field-input" type="url" id="confluence_url" name="confluence_url"
               placeholder="https://confluence.ovhcloud.tools/display/CPO/Private+boot+-+M1" required>
        <p class="field-hint">Paste the page's URL from your browser's address bar (any link format works, including a plain "pageId=" link) — space and title are extracted automatically. Not everything lives in Jira: sections "Deliverables status", "Week summary" and "Risk matrix" on this page are parsed to seed workstreams and pre-fill each weekly report.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="field-group">
        <label class="field-step"><span class="step-num">4.</span> Click "Create" below</label>
        <p class="field-hint">The app will fetch the epic's ETA from Jira, then import your workstreams from the Confluence page. You'll land on your project page a few seconds later — with a clear error message instead of an empty project if something doesn't match the expected format.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="form-actions">
        <a href="/" class="btn-ghost">Cancel</a>
        <button type="submit" class="btn-primary">Create &amp; import epics</button>
      </div>
    </form>
  </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
